WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.267 --> 00:00:02.725
[screaming] Oh, no, my eyes! My eyes!

00:00:07.036 --> 00:00:08.420
[screaming]

00:00:08.420 --> 00:00:11.260
My name is Ian Haworth.
I'm an ex-cult member.

00:00:11.260 --> 00:00:14.090
I escaped from a cult in 1978,

00:00:14.090 --> 00:00:16.160
and today I'm going to
be looking at some clips

00:00:16.160 --> 00:00:18.127
from films all about cults.

00:00:21.301 --> 00:00:24.270
PSI Mind Development Institute Ltd.

00:00:24.270 --> 00:00:26.300
I actually really wanted to quit smoking

00:00:26.300 --> 00:00:27.390
because I'm an asthmatic,

00:00:27.390 --> 00:00:29.150
my doctor had said I should quit,

00:00:29.150 --> 00:00:31.490
and I found there was a course in Toronto,

00:00:31.490 --> 00:00:36.220
so I went to the course
in September of 1978,

00:00:36.220 --> 00:00:38.470
and it was Thursday night, Friday night,

00:00:38.470 --> 00:00:41.420
all day Saturday, all day
Sunday, in a little motel,

00:00:41.420 --> 00:00:43.870
and we went home each
evening after each session.

00:00:43.870 --> 00:00:45.240
And by the end of the course,

00:00:45.240 --> 00:00:46.560
I'd given them all the money I had,

00:00:46.560 --> 00:00:49.500
dedicated my life to it,
and resigned from my job.

00:00:49.500 --> 00:00:52.840
I left the group in October of '78.

00:00:52.840 --> 00:00:54.760
So, after just two and a
half weeks of involvement,

00:00:54.760 --> 00:00:56.896
I went through 11 months of withdrawal.

00:00:57.760 --> 00:01:00.680
The symptoms of withdrawal
are today equated

00:01:00.680 --> 00:01:03.077
quite often with
post-traumatic stress disorder.

00:01:03.077 --> 00:01:05.227
Father: But there comes a day

00:01:06.130 --> 00:01:09.740
when the quality of your life matters more

00:01:09.740 --> 00:01:12.907
than the time you've got left to live.

00:01:13.990 --> 00:01:15.623
This is the end for us.

00:01:17.380 --> 00:01:19.500
Don't wait to be struck down like dogs.

00:01:19.500 --> 00:01:21.700
Take your drink and lay down your life

00:01:21.700 --> 00:01:23.360
with your family.

00:01:23.360 --> 00:01:25.860
Ian: It's depicting Jim Jones

00:01:25.860 --> 00:01:28.118
before he orders people to die

00:01:28.118 --> 00:01:30.276
in Jonestown, Guyana,

00:01:30.276 --> 00:01:32.850
in November of 1978.

00:01:32.850 --> 00:01:35.013
And I saw these bodies on the front page

00:01:35.013 --> 00:01:37.680
of Time magazine and elsewhere,

00:01:37.680 --> 00:01:38.513
and I thought, you know,

00:01:38.513 --> 00:01:40.450
I could have been one of those people.

00:01:40.450 --> 00:01:43.060
I think, for someone viewing it

00:01:43.060 --> 00:01:46.010
without knowing what's gone on prior,

00:01:46.010 --> 00:01:48.182
it will be difficult
for them to understand.

00:01:48.182 --> 00:01:49.693
"Why would you listen to someone saying

00:01:49.693 --> 00:01:51.950
these things? They're idiotic!"

00:01:51.950 --> 00:01:54.260
Yeah, because you're using logic.

00:01:54.260 --> 00:01:57.951
But the people listening to that,

00:01:57.951 --> 00:02:00.120
in Jonestown, Guyana,

00:02:00.120 --> 00:02:02.230
were no longer able to use logic.

00:02:02.230 --> 00:02:03.890
They had been programmed to understand

00:02:03.890 --> 00:02:06.650
that he had a special pipeline to God,

00:02:06.650 --> 00:02:09.940
if he wasn't already God himself.

00:02:09.940 --> 00:02:11.940
And so when he said

00:02:11.940 --> 00:02:15.400
drink the liquid that
was laced with poison,

00:02:15.400 --> 00:02:16.650
they did it.

00:02:16.650 --> 00:02:18.440
Interestingly enough,

00:02:18.440 --> 00:02:21.370
some people did try and run away,

00:02:21.370 --> 00:02:23.030
and were shot to death.

00:02:23.030 --> 00:02:25.660
And if you've got a large
population of people,

00:02:25.660 --> 00:02:27.640
such as they had about 1,000 people,

00:02:27.640 --> 00:02:31.478
you give an instruction
that they are to die,

00:02:32.820 --> 00:02:34.890
in any population of cult members,

00:02:34.890 --> 00:02:35.900
some people are gonna be

00:02:35.900 --> 00:02:39.280
just a little bit closer
to reality than others.

00:02:39.280 --> 00:02:41.130
We had such a good example of this,

00:02:41.130 --> 00:02:42.188
where some people thought,

00:02:42.188 --> 00:02:44.255
"Oh, hang on a minute, what's going on?"

00:02:44.255 --> 00:02:47.100
And they headed for the jungle,

00:02:47.100 --> 00:02:49.440
and a lot of them were shot dead.

00:02:49.440 --> 00:02:51.440
But some made it into the jungle

00:02:51.440 --> 00:02:54.480
and eventually back to
Georgetown, only a handful.

00:02:54.480 --> 00:02:56.640
What I don't like in this little clip

00:02:56.640 --> 00:02:58.650
is that you see very few people,

00:02:58.650 --> 00:03:00.760
because there were
approximately 1,000 people there

00:03:00.760 --> 00:03:02.800
when all of this happened.

00:03:02.800 --> 00:03:05.709
He was wearing dark glasses because,

00:03:05.709 --> 00:03:09.670
the critics would say,
his eyes were bloodshot,

00:03:09.670 --> 00:03:11.550
and he was covering that up.

00:03:11.550 --> 00:03:13.427
But what he told everyone else was

00:03:13.427 --> 00:03:17.118
the light of God in his eyes

00:03:17.118 --> 00:03:18.401
would knock people over

00:03:18.401 --> 00:03:20.510
unless he wore dark glasses.

00:03:20.510 --> 00:03:23.108
I'd give that one a good eight out of 10.

00:03:24.040 --> 00:03:26.097
Dani: I don't know why I'm here, Pelle!

00:03:26.097 --> 00:03:27.480
I don't know why you invited us!

00:03:27.480 --> 00:03:28.849
[stammering] I don't know,
I don't know why I'm here!

00:03:28.849 --> 00:03:30.235
Pelle: OK, OK, OK, OK it's fine.

00:03:30.235 --> 00:03:32.228
Dani: I don't know, and I can't....

00:03:32.228 --> 00:03:33.061
Pelle: Come on.
Dani: No!

00:03:33.061 --> 00:03:34.136
Pelle: Come on, sit down Dani.

00:03:34.136 --> 00:03:35.294
Dani, please.

00:03:35.294 --> 00:03:36.960
[Dani crying]
Please sit down.

00:03:36.960 --> 00:03:39.552
Ian: This is a good clip, in my opinion.

00:03:39.552 --> 00:03:42.101
It's a form of love bombing,

00:03:42.101 --> 00:03:45.426
not to recruit someone but to try and

00:03:45.426 --> 00:03:48.557
keep someone in the group at a point where

00:03:48.557 --> 00:03:52.140
their critical faculties
have come back to the fore.

00:03:52.140 --> 00:03:55.610
So you bomb that person with love.

00:03:55.610 --> 00:03:59.520
You surround them with a
lot of hugs and kisses.

00:03:59.520 --> 00:04:01.250
It's as phony as a three-dollar bill.

00:04:01.250 --> 00:04:02.230
It's conditional love,

00:04:02.230 --> 00:04:04.810
conditional on towing the party line.

00:04:04.810 --> 00:04:07.260
Everybody in a cult watches everyone else.

00:04:07.260 --> 00:04:10.540
And if anyone is weakening, or slipping,

00:04:10.540 --> 00:04:13.250
or whatever the terminology might be,

00:04:13.250 --> 00:04:15.595
then they'll pounce on that person

00:04:15.595 --> 00:04:17.980
psychologically and work on them.

00:04:17.980 --> 00:04:20.410
A lot of cults used to
be visually identifiable

00:04:20.410 --> 00:04:21.770
because of their clothing,

00:04:21.770 --> 00:04:26.752
but after the 1970s,

00:04:26.752 --> 00:04:31.752
most groups were much more
difficult to visually identify.

00:04:32.100 --> 00:04:34.933
Very useful clip. I would
give that eight out of 10.

00:04:37.241 --> 00:04:38.856
Lucy [on phone]: But where have you been?

00:04:40.731 --> 00:04:42.293
Martha: Um, I'm not sure.

00:04:42.293 --> 00:04:44.068
I'm...

00:04:44.068 --> 00:04:45.930
upstate, I think.

00:04:45.930 --> 00:04:47.746
Ian: This is such a useful clip,

00:04:47.746 --> 00:04:49.287
as far as I'm concerned.

00:04:49.287 --> 00:04:51.420
When someone becomes a
victim of mind control,

00:04:51.420 --> 00:04:53.460
there's pressure put on the human mind

00:04:53.460 --> 00:04:54.930
and a change occurs.

00:04:54.930 --> 00:04:56.630
You go through a change of personality.

00:04:56.630 --> 00:04:57.490
If this is the real you,

00:04:57.490 --> 00:04:58.880
it's pushed out of action,

00:04:58.880 --> 00:05:00.970
and a new you is created.

00:05:00.970 --> 00:05:03.030
This is such a concern for most cults

00:05:03.030 --> 00:05:06.010
that they'll have a person shadowing you

00:05:06.010 --> 00:05:09.750
so that if you were to
make a phone call home,

00:05:09.750 --> 00:05:11.380
if the group knows about
that ahead of time,

00:05:11.380 --> 00:05:13.820
they'll make sure that
there's somebody with you,

00:05:13.820 --> 00:05:16.538
making sure that you say certain things

00:05:16.538 --> 00:05:19.050
that might even be scripted.

00:05:19.050 --> 00:05:21.862
So that's great. I would give that

00:05:21.862 --> 00:05:25.362
a good solid nine again, out of 10.

00:05:25.362 --> 00:05:27.077
Excellent.

00:05:27.077 --> 00:05:29.913
Dad: There's someone visiting
we want you to talk to.

00:05:29.913 --> 00:05:32.460
We just wanna be sure
you're on the right track.

00:05:32.460 --> 00:05:33.510
Brother: Yeah, we all love you.

00:05:33.510 --> 00:05:35.050
I, I love you.

00:05:35.050 --> 00:05:36.487
[Ruth panting]
Dad: You know we love you.

00:05:37.520 --> 00:05:40.425
Ian: Overall, I was very, very

00:05:40.425 --> 00:05:42.360
concerned about and critical of the film

00:05:42.360 --> 00:05:45.580
because it depicted a deprograming

00:05:45.580 --> 00:05:47.580
that was so far from reality,

00:05:47.580 --> 00:05:50.660
it was just nonsense, but
that clip is a good one.

00:05:50.660 --> 00:05:51.840
The issue of deprograming

00:05:51.840 --> 00:05:53.370
has always been very controversial,

00:05:53.370 --> 00:05:54.587
and what we're talking
about when we talk about

00:05:54.587 --> 00:05:57.727
deprograming is a family
hiring the services

00:05:57.727 --> 00:05:59.590
of somebody who would be involved

00:05:59.590 --> 00:06:03.620
in, shall we say, a form of counseling,

00:06:03.620 --> 00:06:05.830
where the person needs to be detained.

00:06:05.830 --> 00:06:08.610
And that's it. You've got
to really detain the person.

00:06:08.610 --> 00:06:10.050
And so it's always very controversial,

00:06:10.050 --> 00:06:13.260
because families would grab the loved one,

00:06:13.260 --> 00:06:15.150
and the loved one would be taken away

00:06:15.150 --> 00:06:18.140
to what they would normally
describe as a safe house,

00:06:18.140 --> 00:06:21.580
and the deprogrammer would
start to talk to this person,

00:06:21.580 --> 00:06:23.150
and the person wouldn't
be allowed to leave,

00:06:23.150 --> 00:06:25.702
and the average deprograming might take

00:06:25.702 --> 00:06:28.250
two, three, four days,
something like that.

00:06:28.250 --> 00:06:29.316
Brother: He's a great guy, sis.

00:06:29.316 --> 00:06:30.420
[Ruth hyperventilating]
He's real experienced

00:06:30.420 --> 00:06:31.620
in religion and stuff.

00:06:31.620 --> 00:06:32.453
Just three days.

00:06:32.453 --> 00:06:33.630
Just listen to him, yeah?

00:06:35.120 --> 00:06:37.590
Ian: In those cases where
deprogramings did occur,

00:06:37.590 --> 00:06:40.027
and they only accounted for a very small

00:06:40.027 --> 00:06:43.500
minority of cases,

00:06:43.500 --> 00:06:44.710
that was, indeed,

00:06:44.710 --> 00:06:46.450
exactly the sort of
thing that would happen.

00:06:46.450 --> 00:06:48.733
So, I'd give that clip a good nine.

00:06:51.310 --> 00:06:53.200
Rebecca: You having a good day?

00:06:53.200 --> 00:06:54.733
Danny: Who knows?

00:06:54.733 --> 00:06:55.810
Rebecca: I know.

00:06:55.810 --> 00:06:57.500
Danny: You know?

00:06:57.500 --> 00:06:59.840
Rebecca: Have you ever
had the feeling of being

00:06:59.840 --> 00:07:02.488
connected to someone in a way that...

00:07:03.550 --> 00:07:05.446
goes beyond understanding?

00:07:06.780 --> 00:07:08.510
Ian: I think this is a great clip.

00:07:08.510 --> 00:07:11.475
I know when I was in a cult myself

00:07:11.475 --> 00:07:13.860
and I had to go out and meet people,

00:07:13.860 --> 00:07:15.670
I was given two instructions.

00:07:15.670 --> 00:07:18.700
One was, go for people
you're attracted to.

00:07:18.700 --> 00:07:21.440
And two, stay away from space cadets.

00:07:21.440 --> 00:07:23.040
The lady that was talking to me

00:07:23.040 --> 00:07:25.550
to try and get me to go that meeting,

00:07:25.550 --> 00:07:28.160
she was very, very complimentary.

00:07:28.160 --> 00:07:29.862
You know, you can tend
to read a little bit

00:07:29.862 --> 00:07:32.500
more into that than is actually there.

00:07:32.500 --> 00:07:35.220
They'll say anything to get you
to go to that first meeting.

00:07:35.220 --> 00:07:37.012
Very, very good, that particular clip.

00:07:47.164 --> 00:07:48.860
There's a look that some people have

00:07:48.860 --> 00:07:51.340
called the thousand-mile
stare, originally.

00:07:51.340 --> 00:07:53.300
We don't use it very
often in the field now,

00:07:53.300 --> 00:07:56.280
but back in the 1970s,
that's what it was called.

00:07:56.280 --> 00:07:58.360
It was usually associated with someone

00:07:58.360 --> 00:08:00.820
that had been put into a deep trance state

00:08:00.820 --> 00:08:03.280
and was sort of looking straight through

00:08:03.280 --> 00:08:05.810
anybody in front of them.

00:08:05.810 --> 00:08:08.440
Because they had been put
into that state of mind

00:08:08.440 --> 00:08:10.587
by a cult recruiter standing about

00:08:10.587 --> 00:08:12.780
this far and locking eyes on them.

00:08:12.780 --> 00:08:15.172
Gotta be another nine out of 10, for sure.

00:08:16.268 --> 00:08:17.488
Lancaster: Could you
answer the next series of

00:08:17.488 --> 00:08:19.430
questions without blinking your eyes?

00:08:19.430 --> 00:08:20.750
Freddie: Yes.
Lancaster: Without fear

00:08:20.750 --> 00:08:22.604
and hesitation, answer
as quickly as you can.

00:08:22.604 --> 00:08:24.128
Freddie: Sure.

00:08:24.128 --> 00:08:25.420
Lancaster: Have you killed anyone?

00:08:25.420 --> 00:08:26.253
Freddie: No.

00:08:26.253 --> 00:08:27.560
Lancaster: Maybe?
Freddie: Not me.

00:08:27.560 --> 00:08:29.540
Lancaster: Have you killed anyone?

00:08:29.540 --> 00:08:30.373
Freddie: Yes.

00:08:30.373 --> 00:08:31.863
Lancaster: Who?
Freddie: Japs in war.

00:08:32.830 --> 00:08:34.380
Lancaster: Do you regret this?
Freddie: No.

00:08:34.380 --> 00:08:36.370
Ian: If it's trying to show

00:08:36.370 --> 00:08:38.256
that they can dig out all kinds of things

00:08:38.256 --> 00:08:40.560
from your past that can
be used against you,

00:08:40.560 --> 00:08:42.330
then that's good as well.

00:08:42.330 --> 00:08:44.300
Normally when one thinks
of a cult environment,

00:08:44.300 --> 00:08:46.150
one thinks of a group of people,

00:08:46.150 --> 00:08:49.690
and the whole group is usually
working on the individual.

00:08:49.690 --> 00:08:52.010
But in the group that that's portraying,

00:08:52.010 --> 00:08:53.990
there are certainly one-on-one sessions

00:08:53.990 --> 00:08:57.840
that aren't terribly dissimilar
to what was shown there.

00:08:57.840 --> 00:09:00.496
This is, presumably, trying to show

00:09:00.496 --> 00:09:04.150
the early days of what led to a situation

00:09:04.150 --> 00:09:06.240
where people are holding
a couple of tin cans

00:09:06.240 --> 00:09:10.170
that are attached to
wires and run to a meter

00:09:10.170 --> 00:09:14.280
that is supposed to
measure one's stress level.

00:09:14.280 --> 00:09:17.000
We talk about techniques
of psychological coercion

00:09:17.000 --> 00:09:19.050
being used against the individual,

00:09:19.050 --> 00:09:22.333
and the average, normal, healthy person

00:09:22.333 --> 00:09:25.299
is broken down and completely controlled

00:09:25.299 --> 00:09:26.710
in a matter of three or four days.

00:09:26.710 --> 00:09:28.057
That's all it takes.

00:09:28.057 --> 00:09:29.843
Producer: Out of 10,

00:09:29.843 --> 00:09:31.388
what you would give that one

00:09:31.388 --> 00:09:33.388
on a scale of one to 10 out of realism?

00:09:34.250 --> 00:09:35.631
Ian: Five or six.

00:09:39.029 --> 00:09:41.628
[people shouting]

00:09:41.628 --> 00:09:42.926
Edward: [yelling] What
is that, what is that?

00:09:42.926 --> 00:09:44.290
What is it?

00:09:44.290 --> 00:09:46.312
Oh, no, not the bees!
[bees buzzing]

00:09:46.312 --> 00:09:47.578
Not the bees!

00:09:47.578 --> 00:09:49.530
[screams]

00:09:49.530 --> 00:09:50.960
Oh, no, my eyes!

00:09:50.960 --> 00:09:52.092
My eyes!

00:09:52.092 --> 00:09:55.100
[screaming]

00:09:55.100 --> 00:09:58.090
Ian: If we look at this clip in terms of

00:09:58.090 --> 00:10:02.730
is it possible for a cult to harm someone

00:10:02.730 --> 00:10:05.210
who comes in to investigate,

00:10:05.210 --> 00:10:06.920
no question about it.

00:10:06.920 --> 00:10:09.353
Cults will do terrible things

00:10:09.353 --> 00:10:10.620
to their own members as well,

00:10:10.620 --> 00:10:12.460
in terms of beatings.

00:10:12.460 --> 00:10:15.040
Would it be done in front of the others?

00:10:15.040 --> 00:10:16.530
Possibly.

00:10:16.530 --> 00:10:19.240
Needn't be, it could be
done quietly elsewhere,

00:10:19.240 --> 00:10:22.480
so the rest of the members aren't aware.

00:10:22.480 --> 00:10:24.021
I remember, I gave evidence

00:10:24.021 --> 00:10:26.180
in a court case once in Canada

00:10:26.180 --> 00:10:28.180
and afterwards the judge said:

00:10:28.180 --> 00:10:29.755
"Should I be concerned

00:10:31.340 --> 00:10:34.860
about this particular
cult that's on trial here?

00:10:34.860 --> 00:10:37.110
Is it possible that the
cult leader will order

00:10:37.110 --> 00:10:38.769
something to happen to me?"

00:10:39.620 --> 00:10:42.370
And I said, "Well, Your Honor, if you say,

00:10:42.370 --> 00:10:44.920
'Is it possible?' the answer is yes."

00:10:44.920 --> 00:10:48.045
If the cult leaders control

00:10:48.045 --> 00:10:49.328
the minds of the members

00:10:49.328 --> 00:10:52.030
and then fill their heads with something

00:10:52.030 --> 00:10:54.470
of a pagan-related nature,

00:10:54.470 --> 00:10:56.110
then that would make sense.

00:10:56.110 --> 00:10:58.835
The key issue,

00:10:58.835 --> 00:11:00.951
rather than it being
pagan or something else,

00:11:00.951 --> 00:11:02.200
is the mind control first.

00:11:02.200 --> 00:11:04.890
That's what comes first
in every situation.

00:11:04.890 --> 00:11:08.640
And then you can get the
members to do anything for you.

00:11:08.640 --> 00:11:10.265
I'll give that one a six.

00:11:12.140 --> 00:11:14.282
David: You got your law
degree from Harvard.

00:11:15.300 --> 00:11:17.790
Was that enough for you, Wayne?

00:11:17.790 --> 00:11:18.748
Wayne: Nope.

00:11:20.100 --> 00:11:24.028
David: Steve. Professor of theology.

00:11:24.028 --> 00:11:24.953
Amazing.

00:11:26.660 --> 00:11:27.968
Ian: In a typical cult,

00:11:27.968 --> 00:11:30.612
the leader will be charismatic,

00:11:30.612 --> 00:11:32.503
and so that's a good depiction

00:11:32.503 --> 00:11:34.880
of a charismatic leader there.

00:11:34.880 --> 00:11:37.055
What I also like is that

00:11:37.055 --> 00:11:40.280
he's singling out individual
people in the group

00:11:40.280 --> 00:11:42.270
and talking about their academic

00:11:42.270 --> 00:11:43.728
or professional backgrounds,

00:11:43.728 --> 00:11:46.403
and that is so typical as well.

00:11:46.403 --> 00:11:51.280
You find in cults, they've
recruited students,

00:11:51.280 --> 00:11:53.805
doctors, lawyers,

00:11:53.805 --> 00:11:57.290
businesspeople, you name it.

00:11:57.290 --> 00:11:58.760
Cults recruit people,

00:11:58.760 --> 00:12:01.810
and a lot of them are professional people.

00:12:01.810 --> 00:12:03.760
What we saw in that clip was David Koresh,

00:12:03.760 --> 00:12:07.890
he was being depicted by the actor there,

00:12:07.890 --> 00:12:10.560
talking to the members of the group,

00:12:10.560 --> 00:12:13.640
and they were based in Waco, Texas,

00:12:13.640 --> 00:12:16.384
and they'd managed to amass

00:12:16.384 --> 00:12:19.211
quite a lot of weaponry over the years,

00:12:19.211 --> 00:12:23.610
and they weren't keen on visitors.

00:12:23.610 --> 00:12:26.680
At one point in time, in the 1990s,

00:12:26.680 --> 00:12:30.070
the authorities laid siege,
basically, to the place.

00:12:30.070 --> 00:12:33.500
Shots were fired from both sides.

00:12:33.500 --> 00:12:36.340
A lot of officers, with the authorities,

00:12:36.340 --> 00:12:39.060
were shot and killed; others were injured.

00:12:39.060 --> 00:12:43.320
A part of the building
was seen to be on fire.

00:12:43.320 --> 00:12:46.220
And I remember doing a
commentary at the time,

00:12:46.220 --> 00:12:51.220
as it was happening, for one
of the television stations.

00:12:51.492 --> 00:12:53.784
And only one guy jumped out of a window.

00:12:54.700 --> 00:12:57.357
And the rest stayed inside and...

00:12:58.770 --> 00:13:00.360
and died.

00:13:00.360 --> 00:13:03.290
And that is so typical of
what you would do in a cult,

00:13:03.290 --> 00:13:05.860
because if the leader says,
"Stay in and we'll die

00:13:05.860 --> 00:13:08.090
and then go to heaven,"
or whatever he's saying,

00:13:08.090 --> 00:13:09.490
then that's what you do.

00:13:09.490 --> 00:13:12.470
Yeah, as far as the setting goes,

00:13:12.470 --> 00:13:13.390
that seemed to be accurate.

00:13:13.390 --> 00:13:15.355
They had a building very much like

00:13:15.355 --> 00:13:17.760
what we saw in the clip there.

00:13:17.760 --> 00:13:19.230
He doesn't look terribly different

00:13:19.230 --> 00:13:21.990
from the man in real life, David Koresh,

00:13:21.990 --> 00:13:24.040
so, yeah, useful clip.

00:13:24.040 --> 00:13:26.077
Seven out of 10. [laughs]

00:13:26.077 --> 00:13:27.380
Patrick: Would you like
to buy some flowers?

00:13:27.380 --> 00:13:28.280
They're fresh cut.

00:13:28.280 --> 00:13:29.450
Man in suit: No, thanks.

00:13:29.450 --> 00:13:30.283
Patrick: For your wife?

00:13:30.283 --> 00:13:31.810
Or your girlfriend.

00:13:31.810 --> 00:13:33.290
It's for a good cause.

00:13:33.290 --> 00:13:35.190
We're a Christian group raising money

00:13:35.190 --> 00:13:37.420
for a drug-rehabilitation center.

00:13:37.420 --> 00:13:38.870
David: You lied to that man, Patrick.

00:13:38.870 --> 00:13:40.880
Patrick: I brought in $20 for Father.

00:13:40.880 --> 00:13:42.030
David: It's mine!

00:13:42.030 --> 00:13:43.270
Ian: I love this clip.

00:13:43.270 --> 00:13:46.200
One group calls it heavenly deception.

00:13:46.200 --> 00:13:49.267
Another group calls it
transcendental trickery.

00:13:49.267 --> 00:13:51.720
And the whole film is
based on a true story.

00:13:51.720 --> 00:13:53.250
So, what do they sell at the doors?

00:13:53.250 --> 00:13:55.550
It can be anything. Cacti, flowers,

00:13:55.550 --> 00:13:58.920
it can be little painted
something or others.

00:13:58.920 --> 00:14:01.440
One group is known for selling paintings,

00:14:01.440 --> 00:14:03.430
just absolutely anything,

00:14:03.430 --> 00:14:05.350
and that can change from week to week

00:14:05.350 --> 00:14:07.240
as the leader would want it.

00:14:07.240 --> 00:14:08.160
10 out of 10.

00:14:08.160 --> 00:14:09.225
Yeah.

00:14:19.640 --> 00:14:22.750
Some cults do have schools.

00:14:22.750 --> 00:14:24.540
The standard of education they get

00:14:24.540 --> 00:14:26.610
is another matter altogether.

00:14:26.610 --> 00:14:29.840
Normally in a cult,
children are a problem.

00:14:29.840 --> 00:14:32.750
Children are often
treated very, very harshly

00:14:32.750 --> 00:14:34.760
to keep them quiet.

00:14:34.760 --> 00:14:39.000
And if you keep them
away from their parents,

00:14:39.000 --> 00:14:42.030
then the parents aren't
gonna be distracted at all

00:14:42.030 --> 00:14:43.400
if you're programming them

00:14:43.400 --> 00:14:45.920
or doing whatever you're
doing with the parents.

00:14:45.920 --> 00:14:49.310
It helps to break down the bonds as well,

00:14:49.310 --> 00:14:51.750
because the last thing a cult leader wants

00:14:51.750 --> 00:14:55.225
is for a cult member having

00:14:55.225 --> 00:14:58.095
a loving relationship with someone else

00:14:58.095 --> 00:15:01.128
and for that loving relationship

00:15:01.128 --> 00:15:02.678
to start to interfere with the control

00:15:02.678 --> 00:15:05.160
that he or she, the cult leader, has.

00:15:05.160 --> 00:15:06.026
Seven out of 10.

00:15:06.026 --> 00:15:07.092
No problem.

00:15:08.410 --> 00:15:09.740
Sadie: What did Charlie say?

00:15:09.740 --> 00:15:13.050
Tex: He said, "Go to Terry's old house

00:15:13.050 --> 00:15:14.775
and kill everybody in there."

00:15:18.200 --> 00:15:20.143
Ian: Charles Manson ran a group called

00:15:20.143 --> 00:15:22.740
the family, the Manson family.

00:15:22.740 --> 00:15:25.306
When they see a tragedy in terms of

00:15:25.306 --> 00:15:27.247
people being murdered,

00:15:27.247 --> 00:15:29.470
as was the case with the Manson family,

00:15:29.470 --> 00:15:32.300
and they can relate to that
as a problem, and rightly,

00:15:32.300 --> 00:15:33.500
I think some people think, "Oh, well,

00:15:33.500 --> 00:15:35.940
that's just an extreme example

00:15:35.940 --> 00:15:37.890
of what we're talking about
in the world of cults."

00:15:37.890 --> 00:15:39.280
For me, it's not.

00:15:39.280 --> 00:15:41.190
Going around murdering people

00:15:41.190 --> 00:15:43.706
usually gets the police involved,

00:15:43.706 --> 00:15:45.100
and quite rightly.

00:15:45.100 --> 00:15:46.416
So, most cult leaders don't

00:15:46.416 --> 00:15:47.807
get you to do that sort of thing.

00:15:47.807 --> 00:15:49.260
They get you to go and lie to people

00:15:49.260 --> 00:15:51.912
about fundraising activities,

00:15:51.912 --> 00:15:53.340
and so you bring in a lot of money,

00:15:53.340 --> 00:15:54.890
and you bring in a lot of people.

00:15:54.890 --> 00:15:57.390
I'd give that something like a seven.

